For those of you who think that pudding farming was abusive... :-P
Here's another item-producing technique involving killing vault guards:

- Find a vault, preferably on a level with an altar for B/C/U'ing, and
  dig through to it.
- Have a means of infinite instant kills, preferably with no penalty for
  killing peacefuls (pet purple worms are my current favorite)
- Have enough food to not starve (or wear =oSD)
- (Optionally) have a chest or box to stash useless stuff in
- Repeat until you get an aneurysm:
	- Sit in vault (with pet purple worm) and wait until guard shows
	  up (100. or 100s works well)
	- Anger guard by vehemently claiming you are Croesus (for some
	  reason, unless the guard is angered, you get no items out of
	  him---also, angering him seems to not seal off the corridor
	  even though the game claims it closes up)
	- Wait one turn and let pet do the dirty job (Burrrrp!)
	- Collect valuable items, stash away useless armor in chest/box
	  (for those neatniks among you)

If repeated often enough, you'll get a lot of potions, scrolls, and
wands. (I'm not sure if every possible potion will be generated, but so
far I've gotten a good variety.)

I stumbled upon this method while trying to play my first extinctionist
character (Q: "How do you kill 255 vault guards without being penalized
for killing peacefuls?" A: "Acquire a pet purple worm.") :-)


